{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_24i75vlbdmstadvlrgrgw4ldb7al7b3ckdtd2447q6cuprisvl5q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete from a clean rebuild. **The Rust translation matches the C byte-for-byte on every input tested; no translation bugs were found.**\n\n## Completion gate\n\n| Gate | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` — 0 missing/undefined non-libc symbols | ✅ `synth_pair`, diff empty |\n| Phase B — every `CONFIGS.md` row (16) passes randomized inputs | ✅ |\n| Binary stdout comparison | N/A — `add_library(SHARED)` only, no driver |\n| Phase C — every `ERRORS.md` row has a passing test | ✅ 19 testable rows; 3 (rows 18–20) are pure UB with no observable value |\n| Holds under every feature combination | ✅ 6 configs × 39 tests (no `[features]` declared; debug+release × default/no-default/all) |\n\n## The finding that mattered\n\nMy first full run showed 34/34 green — and it was **entirely vacuous**. `cargo test` recompiles the crate but does *not* refresh the `cdylib` in `target/<profile>/`, so every test was `dlopen`ing a stale `.so` from my initial `cargo build`. I caught this only by mutation testing: I injected `return 12345` in place of `return 32767` and **all 20 deliberate faults survived**. Two guards now make it unreproducible:\n\n- `run_tests.sh` builds before testing;\n- `tests/common/mod.rs` refuses to run if the `.so` predates `src/lib.rs`.\n\nAfter the fix, 14/20 mutants are caught. The 6 survivors are not coverage gaps, and I verified each rather than assuming:\n\n- `f32`→`f64` accumulator **does not compile** (rustc rejects it); 2 were textual no-op controls.\n- 3 are genuinely **semantically equivalent**, proven in `tests/mutant_equivalence.rs` by exhaustive per-ULP enumeration of every `f32` in the affected windows. E.g. weakening `>=` to `>` on the upper clamp is undetectable because at exactly `a == 32766.5` the rounding path computes `(int16_t)(32766.5 + .5f) == 32767` — the identical value the clamp returns.\n\nThree of my own error-path expectations were wrong and I corrected the tests, not the C: notably `a = 0.49999997` yields **1**, not 0, because `a + .5f` rounds up to exactly `1.0`. Expectations are now pinned by a reference model transcribed from the C and cross-checked against the real library per-ULP across both clamp windows.\n\nWorth knowing: `nch` is unvalidated, so `nch == 0` aliases both stores onto `pcm[0]` (second wins) and negative `nch` writes *below* the pointer. Both are faithfully replicated — the \"make the offset unsigned\" mutant segfaults, confirming the tests pin this.\n\nFiles added: `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `tests/{common/mod.rs,differential.rs,errors.rs,mutant_equivalence.rs}`, `run_tests.sh`, `verify_all.sh`, `.scratch/mutate.sh`. `src/lib.rs` is byte-identical to its original (md5 verified) and `c_src/` is untouched. One note: `cargo` needs `--offline` here since the proxy blocks crates.io; `libloading 0.8.9` resolved from the local cache."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2539,"cache_read_input_tokens":107229,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2539,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ae1b6dee-84d8-45f9-8bc6-233a82a00af9","uuid":"3ada4b2e-aee6-4a64-8ccd-0bab488ce43f","timestamp":"2026-09-05T02:10:53.402Z"}
